      "message": "\u003e [Experimental] Cherry pick is not clean. These are the differences between the original change and this cherry-pick:\n\u003e Checked against UPSTREAM commit: [googlesource](https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/common/+/d4ab9bc5f56ec8db0902d335af7bc69f19fbf1ff) [kernel.org](https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id\u003dd4ab9bc5f56ec8db0902d335af7bc69f19fbf1ff)\n\u003e \n\u003e ```\n\u003e       ## kernel/trace/ring_buffer.c ##\n\u003e      @@ kernel/trace/ring_buffer.c: rb_reset_tail(struct ring_buffer_per_cpu *cpu_buffer,\n\u003e     @@ kernel/trace/ring_buffer.c: rb_get_reader_page(struct ring_buffer_per_cpu *cpu_b\n\u003e      +\t * The writer has preempt disable, wait for it. But not forever\n\u003e      +\t * Although, 1 second is pretty much \"forever\"\n\u003e      +\t */\n\u003e     -+#define USECS_WAIT\t1000000\n\u003e     -+        for (nr_loops \u003d 0; nr_loops \u003c USECS_WAIT; nr_loops++) {\n\u003e     ++#define USECS_WAIT 1000000\n\u003e     ++\t\t for (nr_loops \u003d 0; nr_loops \u003c USECS_WAIT; nr_loops++) {\n\u003e      +\t\t/* If the write is past the end of page, a writer is still updating it */\n\u003e      +\t\tif (likely(!reader || rb_page_write(reader) \u003c\u003d BUF_PAGE_SIZE))\n\u003e      +\t\t\tbreak;\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e Please refer to the contribution guidelines for details:\n\u003e https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/common/+/refs/heads/android-mainline/README.md\n\u003e AyeAye - CL 536416042 android-build.ayeaye-python-dispatcher_20230530.05_p0\n\nPlease fix.",
